§ `Article 56(6): both versions, each tested through its own function, and the dispatcher on each side of 27 July 2026`
-- args: none (the as-enacted and as-amended texts have no gate and no date)
#ASSERT `Art 56(6) as enacted the official who must assess whether the codes of practice cover the obligations and publish the assessment`  EQUALS `Art 51 the AI Office`
#ASSERT `Art 56(6) as amended the official who must assess whether the codes of practice cover the obligations and publish the assessment`  EQUALS `Art 51 the Commission`
#ASSERT `Art 56(6) as enacted the Commission may approve a code of practice by an implementing act`  EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the dispatcher. args: date asked. Chapter V applies from 2 August 2025, before the Omnibus (27 July 2026): both branches are reached.
#ASSERT `Art 56(6) the official who must assess whether the codes of practice cover the obligations and publish the assessment` `Art 55 test the day before the group applies` EQUALS NOTHING
-- as enacted: after the group applies, before the Omnibus
#ASSERT `Art 56(6) the official who must assess whether the codes of practice cover the obligations and publish the assessment` `Art 55 test a later day` EQUALS JUST `Art 51 the AI Office`
-- 26 July 2026, the day before the Omnibus
#ASSERT `Art 56(6) the official who must assess whether the codes of practice cover the obligations and publish the assessment` `Art 55 test the day before the Omnibus` EQUALS JUST `Art 51 the AI Office`
-- 27 July 2026, the day the Omnibus enters into force
#ASSERT `Art 56(6) the official who must assess whether the codes of practice cover the obligations and publish the assessment` `Art 55 test the first day of the Omnibus` EQUALS JUST `Art 51 the Commission`
-- the approval power. args: date asked
