#ASSERT `Art 56(6) the Commission may approve a code of practice by an implementing act and give it a general validity within the Union` `Art 55 test a later day` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 56(6) the Commission may approve a code of practice by an implementing act and give it a general validity within the Union` `Art 55 test the day before the Omnibus` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the text as amended has no such power: silent
#ASSERT `Art 56(6) the Commission may approve a code of practice by an implementing act and give it a general validity within the Union` `Art 55 test the first day of the Omnibus` EQUALS NOTHING
-- rules. Day 0 is the date asked. No time limit and no consequence in either text.
